# 1Password secret references for agentic tooling.
# This file contains NO secret material and is safe to commit and share.
#
# Format:  KEY="<scheme>://<vault>/<item>/<field>"  where the scheme is  op
#   - quote the value when vault or item names contain spaces (they may)
#   - one line per environment variable; several variables may point to the same field
#   - NEVER write a real reference inside a comment: op inject resolves every reference
#     in the file, comments included, and fails the whole file if one cannot be resolved
# Resolve:  secrets-load            (exports into the current shell, one op call, one prompt)
#           secrets-run <command>   (injects into that process only, nothing exported)
#           op read "<reference>"   (single value, ad hoc)
#
# Team convention: vault "ANDRITZ Agents"; one item per real secret; the item below is the
# Foundry resource of one team member, replace it with yours.

# Microsoft Foundry resource key. One key, several consumers: Claude Code (Foundry),
# Codex CLI (env_key AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY), Azure OpenAI SDK/tools, Hindsight agent memory.
# Hindsight with HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=claude-code does not read HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY
# (it authenticates through Claude Code's Foundry variables); the line matters for other providers.
ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_API_KEY="op://ANDRITZ Agents/Foundry AI ECMClaudeCodeBernd/password"
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY="op://ANDRITZ Agents/Foundry AI ECMClaudeCodeBernd/password"
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY="op://ANDRITZ Agents/Foundry AI ECMClaudeCodeBernd/password"

# GitHub fine-grained PAT for the GitHub MCP server (Authorization: Bearer ${GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN}
# in ~/.claude.json). Add the line once the item exists:
#   GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN -> vault "ANDRITZ Agents", item "github-pat-claude-mcp", field credential
